WEBVTT

00:08.230 --> 00:11.930
Sensei, it's time for class.

00:12.460 --> 00:13.950
Yasuda-sensei.

00:15.110 --> 00:17.170
Don't say I didn't try to wake you up.

00:17.170 --> 00:19.650
Uh-oh, we should get back to the classroom.

00:19.650 --> 00:20.870
The bell's about to ring.

00:20.870 --> 00:23.080
Whoa. Yasuda's asleep.

00:25.950 --> 00:28.270
His hair is so soft!

00:28.270 --> 00:29.760
This'll look great.

00:32.190 --> 00:33.940
Yasuda-sensei.

00:33.940 --> 00:35.920
Yasuda-sensei!

00:35.920 --> 00:38.440
Was there someone behind me just now?!

00:38.880 --> 00:41.590
Yup, just a couple of third-years.

00:41.590 --> 00:43.430
I bet they were girls!

00:43.430 --> 00:45.290
How could I miss my chance like that?!

00:45.940 --> 00:46.750
You know...

00:46.750 --> 00:49.960
Damn, my class is already starting.

00:49.960 --> 00:51.570
You know, Yasuda-sensei...

00:51.570 --> 00:52.990
What is it?!

00:55.090 --> 00:57.800
There's something wrong with your head.

00:58.320 --> 00:59.940
I know that!

01:01.550 --> 01:05.330
Why bring it up now?! I'm in a hurry!

01:05.330 --> 01:08.190
I won't argue, but that's not what I meant.

01:08.190 --> 01:09.960
I'm going to class!

02:40.260 --> 02:44.760
<b>Teacher</b>

02:41.070 --> 02:44.760
Your average on the last exams 
was lower than the other classes'.

02:45.520 --> 02:48.770
Write down an answer even if you're unsure.

02:48.770 --> 02:52.770
You left way too many questions blank. 
You're throwing points away.

02:53.220 --> 02:54.860
Are you taking this seriously?

02:56.120 --> 02:58.260
<i>Are </i>you<i> taking this seriously?</i>

02:59.460 --> 03:01.610
Yasuda, I...

03:01.610 --> 03:02.280
What?

03:04.300 --> 03:05.230
<i>Do it!</i>

03:05.230 --> 03:06.660
<i>Ask him, Hori-san!</i>

03:12.460 --> 03:13.920
Never mind.

03:15.070 --> 03:17.920
Your English score was good, as usual.

03:17.920 --> 03:21.120
Oh, um... Thanks.

03:21.120 --> 03:22.440
<i>What do I say?</i>

03:22.440 --> 03:24.430
<i>I can't think of anything.</i>

03:25.480 --> 03:26.990
Does that bother you?

03:26.990 --> 03:27.990
No, sir.

03:29.290 --> 03:30.310
Excuse me!

03:30.310 --> 03:33.310
What is it? Need to use the restroom?

03:33.310 --> 03:35.100
Um, no...

03:35.500 --> 03:37.090
<i>Ask him, Miyamura!</i>

03:37.090 --> 03:38.940
<i>You can do it, Miyamura-kun!</i>

03:40.780 --> 03:42.200
The theme...

03:42.200 --> 03:44.290
Th-The theme?

03:44.290 --> 03:46.640
The theme for today...

03:46.640 --> 03:48.410
What about it?

03:49.810 --> 03:54.210
Does that have anything
to do with what we're discussing?

03:54.210 --> 03:56.670
Er, no. It doesn't, but...

03:56.670 --> 03:57.610
No?

03:57.950 --> 03:58.940
Then sit down.

03:59.440 --> 04:00.440
Okay...

04:00.970 --> 04:04.830
What's going on?
You all seem distracted by something.

04:04.830 --> 04:06.550
<i>It's you!</i>

04:07.700 --> 04:10.720
<i>Oh, no! I overslept, and now I'm late!</i>

04:10.720 --> 04:13.230
<i>What class are we on now?</i>

04:14.310 --> 04:16.430
I'm sorry for being late!

04:16.430 --> 04:18.480
So you finally made it, Yoshikawa.

04:30.250 --> 04:31.850
What gives, Yasuda?

04:31.850 --> 04:34.230
You gotta stop! I can't!

04:37.870 --> 04:39.530
I can't hold it back anymore!

04:39.530 --> 04:42.010
Lookin' cute today, Yasuda!

04:43.280 --> 04:45.140
What's gotten into you all?

04:45.140 --> 04:46.590
I look cute?

04:46.590 --> 04:48.670
Have a look, Yasuda.

04:51.270 --> 04:53.240
What is this?!

04:53.240 --> 04:54.990
How did you not notice?

04:54.990 --> 04:56.880
You can't fool us!

04:59.420 --> 05:00.690
Honestly...

05:01.120 --> 05:04.100
If they're going to do that, 
I want it done while I'm awake!

05:04.100 --> 05:07.320
I want to be able to enjoy
 teenage girls playing with my hair!

05:07.320 --> 05:09.760
<i>There really is something 
wrong with his head.</i>

05:09.760 --> 05:12.260
That was a rare opportunity to...

05:12.580 --> 05:14.580
Reference Room

05:12.580 --> 05:14.580
Science Room

05:12.580 --> 05:14.580
Library

05:15.030 --> 05:19.010
Terajima-sensei, do you know 
where the resource room key is?

05:19.010 --> 05:22.590
I don't. Try asking the one
who's in charge of it.

05:22.590 --> 05:25.840
And who would that be?

05:26.310 --> 05:28.460
Nakamine-sensei, I believe.

05:29.020 --> 05:32.570
Come to think of it, I think 
he used the room yesterday.

05:36.410 --> 05:37.980
Nakamine-sensei!

05:40.740 --> 05:43.300
Please return the resource room key.

05:44.940 --> 05:48.040
I put it back yesterday.

05:48.040 --> 05:49.540
It isn't there.

05:49.990 --> 05:51.350
But I put it back.

05:51.350 --> 05:52.620
It's not there.

05:53.090 --> 05:54.920
That's odd...

05:55.970 --> 05:57.080
Oh.

05:57.080 --> 06:00.050
Oh, it was in my pocket.

06:00.470 --> 06:02.040
My bad.

06:02.040 --> 06:05.340
<i>Why is </i>he<i> in charge of the key?</i>

06:05.340 --> 06:08.100
Man, I'm glad we found it.

06:09.550 --> 06:11.820
You just dropped a different key.

06:13.430 --> 06:16.690
My bicycle key!
I thought I lost it over the summer.

06:16.690 --> 06:18.180
O-Over the summer?

06:18.180 --> 06:19.940
It's winter!

06:20.380 --> 06:22.030
Thank you.

06:22.030 --> 06:24.320
Now I can start riding my bike again.

06:24.600 --> 06:27.190
I didn't really do anything...

06:27.520 --> 06:29.730
No need to be humble.

06:29.730 --> 06:33.700
<i>Maybe we should entrust
the key to someone else.</i>

06:34.030 --> 06:37.280
Do you have any other keys on you?

06:37.280 --> 06:39.130
I wonder...

06:40.210 --> 06:41.950
Hey, it's Yasuda.

06:41.950 --> 06:43.840
Who's that other teacher?

06:43.840 --> 06:45.560
Nakamine-sensei.

06:45.560 --> 06:47.420
Remember? The physics teacher.

06:51.390 --> 06:53.640
Whoa!

06:54.140 --> 06:56.110
How does your pocket do that?

06:56.110 --> 06:57.420
Was that a magic trick?

06:57.420 --> 06:58.910
That's a lot of keys!

06:58.910 --> 07:01.520
Huh? Oh, thanks.

07:02.250 --> 07:05.270
I could do that too if I tried!

07:05.640 --> 07:08.210
You don't need to get 
competitive about it, Yasuda.

07:08.210 --> 07:10.780
No, I'm serious! I could totally do that!

07:12.610 --> 07:14.840
Sensei, there was another key over here.

07:14.840 --> 07:19.800
Oh, thank you. I would've been
in trouble again without that.

07:20.780 --> 07:21.660
Huh?

07:25.140 --> 07:28.190
Th-The resource room key is gone.

07:28.190 --> 07:30.570
Nakamine-sensei!

07:28.550 --> 07:30.970
<b>Loop</b>

07:42.820 --> 07:44.380
Sensei!

07:45.230 --> 07:46.870
You dropped these.

07:48.230 --> 07:50.130
Oh, silly me.

07:50.130 --> 07:51.430
Thank you.

07:51.430 --> 07:54.890
Sensei, you might have a hole in your pocket.

07:55.520 --> 07:58.370
What? There's no way...

08:04.780 --> 08:08.250
Sensei, I have a sewing kit.

08:08.820 --> 08:10.180
You don't say!

08:10.510 --> 08:12.260
<b>Home Economics</b>

08:13.840 --> 08:16.760
You're quite skilled with 
your hands, young lady.

08:16.760 --> 08:20.320
Sensei, I'm Yoshikawa from class 3-1.

08:20.320 --> 08:22.650
R-Right...

08:22.650 --> 08:24.190
Sorry.

08:24.190 --> 08:28.070
I don't teach class 3-1.

08:28.720 --> 08:32.070
But you taught us as first-years.

08:32.540 --> 08:34.260
Did you forget?

08:34.820 --> 08:40.260
I've had trouble remembering 
faces and names since I was young.

08:41.580 --> 08:45.070
But I remember you.

08:57.050 --> 08:58.310
It's an affair.

08:59.080 --> 09:01.150
But it's Nakamine-sensei...

09:01.150 --> 09:03.350
But it's <i>Nakamine-sensei</i>!

09:03.350 --> 09:04.410
How'd he do it?

09:04.410 --> 09:07.420
How'd he get a teenage girl alone
doing that for him?

09:07.420 --> 09:09.950
Shut up. How should I know? Drop dead.

09:09.950 --> 09:11.990
I don't like hearing
you say that so casually.

09:11.990 --> 09:14.610
This is no time to start
acting like a real teacher!

09:15.220 --> 09:21.120
Gotta say, I never expected
 Yoshikawa to carry a sewing set.

09:21.120 --> 09:23.870
I had no idea either. What's more...

09:25.180 --> 09:28.020
{fb}Toru, you're missing a button.

09:28.020 --> 09:30.140
{fb}Oh, I didn't notice.

09:30.140 --> 09:33.140
{fb}Honestly. Make sure you sew it back on.

09:34.100 --> 09:38.610
That's how she treated me this summer!

09:38.610 --> 09:41.190
Sounds like she has
no love for you whatsoever.

09:41.190 --> 09:44.270
You might as well be "Rando A" to her.

09:44.270 --> 09:49.020
Don't talk like you know how she feels
when you don't, you sexual harasser!

09:49.020 --> 09:52.270
Then what about Nakamine-sensei?
What about him, huh?!

09:52.270 --> 09:58.070
Nakamine doesn't give off even a whiff of 
ulterior motives, criminality, or indecency.

09:58.070 --> 09:59.930
You, on the other hand...

09:59.930 --> 10:03.510
What?! I have only the purest intentions!

10:03.510 --> 10:04.550
Huh?!

10:04.550 --> 10:05.400
Wow!

10:07.910 --> 10:11.500
You sewed it right up. Thank you so much.

10:12.170 --> 10:15.340
Let me know if you ever get another hole.

10:15.340 --> 10:17.320
And take better care of those keys!

10:18.830 --> 10:23.040
Yoshikawa-san, do you always 
have a needle and thread on you?

10:23.040 --> 10:24.430
Yeah, sure do.

10:25.030 --> 10:28.310
There's a certain someone 
who keeps losing his buttons.

10:28.820 --> 10:31.820
But he doesn't tell me when it happens.

10:31.820 --> 10:34.370
Oh, that's really too bad.

10:34.730 --> 10:39.540
Say, to show my appreciation, 
can I get you something to drink?

10:39.540 --> 10:42.490
No, thanks. I'm still working on this.

10:43.230 --> 10:45.490
Hey, instead, Sensei, 
let me see your hand.

10:49.310 --> 10:51.500
What are they talking about?

10:51.840 --> 10:53.250
How should I know?

10:53.250 --> 10:55.890
She finished mending...

11:13.230 --> 11:14.440
Toru?

11:14.440 --> 11:15.430
Oh my.

11:20.470 --> 11:23.160
What were you doing back there?

11:25.060 --> 11:26.440
What do you mean?

11:26.780 --> 11:28.100
With his hands.

11:28.100 --> 11:29.290
Oh, that?

11:29.290 --> 11:30.870
I was doing a palm reading.

11:32.040 --> 11:33.990
What brought that on?

11:33.990 --> 11:35.560
I'm into it lately. It's neat.

11:35.560 --> 11:37.380
I can read yours, too!

11:37.380 --> 11:38.860
Nah, I'll pass.

11:38.860 --> 11:40.740
It's fine. I don't mind.

11:50.000 --> 11:52.020
Your palm lines are so faint!

11:52.020 --> 11:53.950
Just like Nakamine-sensei's!

11:53.950 --> 11:56.440
<i>That's</i> what you were looking at?!

11:56.440 --> 11:59.130
Aren't you supposed to tell me how lucky I am?

11:59.130 --> 12:01.230
I can't tell that.

12:01.230 --> 12:03.650
Go watch your horoscope on the news.

12:03.650 --> 12:05.450
Talk about a total cop out.

12:06.310 --> 12:09.580
Listen, have you read anyone else's palms?

12:09.890 --> 12:11.090
Nope.

12:11.090 --> 12:14.200
Oh, I did look at Hori's.
Her lines were really easy to see.

12:14.200 --> 12:15.160
Why do you ask?

12:15.160 --> 12:17.940
I just don't want anyone
thinking you're a weirdo.

12:19.350 --> 12:20.920
Not that I do.

12:26.410 --> 12:30.320
Wait, are you saying you think I'm weird?!

12:30.320 --> 12:31.480
<i>No!</i>

12:31.480 --> 12:34.770
I'm not a weirdo! I'm not!

12:34.770 --> 12:35.970
I know.

12:35.970 --> 12:37.230
Ishikawa!

12:37.660 --> 12:40.730
Miyamura says he's in for tomorrow!

12:40.730 --> 12:43.990
Nice! Where should we go, then?

12:45.160 --> 12:48.390
What if we go find an empty classroom, bro?

12:48.390 --> 12:49.740
Who are calling "bro"?

12:49.740 --> 12:51.830
Ooh, what's this? Lemme in on it!

12:53.460 --> 12:56.250
Just a little guy fun!

12:56.650 --> 12:57.650
Sounds dumb.

12:57.650 --> 12:58.190
What?!

13:07.590 --> 13:10.360
I had a hard time sneaking this in here.

13:12.100 --> 13:14.730
Talk about huge...

13:14.730 --> 13:16.770
We all know bigger is better.

13:16.770 --> 13:24.650
<b>Student Council</b>

13:17.280 --> 13:19.680
I think looks are important, too.

13:19.680 --> 13:23.080
No way. Size is where the romance lies.

13:25.420 --> 13:27.860
Hello, young adolescent boys!

13:27.860 --> 13:31.840
What do we have here
that's got you all so... excited...

13:34.090 --> 13:36.540
Where do you live, Yasuda?

13:37.060 --> 13:39.670
Why? Are you going to come
burn my place down?

13:39.670 --> 13:41.580
No, I'm just interested.

13:41.580 --> 13:44.920
You don't need to be interested 
in where your teachers live.

13:44.920 --> 13:50.930
<b>Student Counseling</b>

13:45.440 --> 13:47.750
And besides, you three are in trouble.

13:47.750 --> 13:49.000
Do you get that?

13:49.000 --> 13:50.930
Sorry.

13:51.310 --> 13:56.130
But school policy doesn't 
forbid having cake in a classroom.

13:56.130 --> 13:59.190
A whole cake is just too much.

13:59.190 --> 14:03.020
Come to think of it, you live 
pretty close to school, right?

14:03.020 --> 14:05.840
I remember sending you a New Year's card.

14:07.450 --> 14:09.530
Are you planning to visit?!

14:09.530 --> 14:13.200
You'd better not! And we're 
still talking about the cake!

14:13.950 --> 14:16.100
We don't care about the cake anymore.

14:16.100 --> 14:18.240
We want to know how you live.

14:18.240 --> 14:19.960
You're a little <i>too</i> honest.

14:20.280 --> 14:22.320
Do you live by yourself?

14:22.320 --> 14:25.210
Huh? Well, you could say that...

14:25.530 --> 14:26.760
Got a girlfriend?

14:26.760 --> 14:27.740
No.

14:27.740 --> 14:30.200
Why does that matter anyway?

14:30.200 --> 14:31.810
Because, you know...

14:31.810 --> 14:34.740
You always go around saying how 
much you like high school girls.

14:34.740 --> 14:37.860
If you had a perfectly normal, 
uninteresting girlfriend...

14:36.810 --> 14:40.230
<b>Perfectly normal girlfriend</b>

14:36.810 --> 14:40.230
<b>Yasuda's perfectly 
normal girlfriend (pending)</b>

14:37.860 --> 14:38.970
I'd be disappointed.

14:38.970 --> 14:40.230
"Uninteresting"?

14:40.230 --> 14:42.000
Ah, yeah, I get that.

14:42.490 --> 14:45.170
If he had a girlfriend, 
that alone would be a shock.

14:45.170 --> 14:45.920
Right?

14:45.920 --> 14:48.740
I said I don't, so you're safe.

14:49.240 --> 14:54.530
Yasuda, let me know if you ever get a
perfectly normal and uninteresting girlfriend.

14:51.280 --> 14:56.870
<b>Perfectly normal girlfriend</b>

14:51.280 --> 14:56.870
<b>Yasuda's perfectly 
normal girlfriend (pending)
Has no hobbies</b>

14:54.530 --> 14:56.870
What exactly are you going for here?

14:57.330 --> 14:59.310
Don't you want to get married?

14:59.310 --> 15:01.500
I don't have anyone <i>to</i> marry.

15:01.500 --> 15:02.630
Weren't you listening?

15:03.160 --> 15:04.580
You should do it.

15:04.930 --> 15:07.840
Marry your super-normal,
completely uninteresting girlfriend.

15:05.210 --> 15:10.130
<b>Perfectly normal girlfriend</b>

15:05.210 --> 15:10.130
<b>Yasuda's perfectly 
normal girlfriend (pending)
Has no hobbies
Her friends are all getting
 married recently</b>

15:07.840 --> 15:10.130
Seriously, who the hell are you talking about?

15:10.610 --> 15:14.550
I mean, I just don't want Nakamine-sensei 
to get married before I do.

15:14.550 --> 15:16.910
<i>He's really fixated on Nakamine.</i>

15:18.230 --> 15:21.170
Damn it, I'm fraternizing with students!

15:21.170 --> 15:24.010
I'd love to see where you live.

15:24.010 --> 15:25.080
Yeah!

15:25.080 --> 15:26.650
You jerks aren't welcome!

15:27.090 --> 15:30.000
However, if you bring some girls, 
I'll allow you in!

15:30.000 --> 15:32.700
Miyamura, you bring Hori! 
Ishikawa, you bring Yoshikawa!

15:32.700 --> 15:35.160
Iura, you bring Ayasaki and Kono!

15:35.530 --> 15:36.710
Huh?

15:36.710 --> 15:38.080
Then forget it.

15:38.080 --> 15:43.670
Hey, what happened to your enthusiasm?

15:40.080 --> 15:43.670
<b>I wanna see where you live!</b>

15:44.010 --> 15:45.510
You're the worst.

15:45.510 --> 15:47.800
I'm not sending you 
a New Year's card next year.

15:47.800 --> 15:49.050
I wasn't expecting one.

15:49.490 --> 15:51.900
I don't know what you're thinking,

15:51.900 --> 15:55.200
but those two don't have any 
strong feelings toward me!

15:55.200 --> 15:56.670
Oh, I see.

15:56.670 --> 15:57.810
Sorry.

15:57.810 --> 16:01.100
Now, back to the cake...

16:06.310 --> 16:07.590
Forget it.

16:07.590 --> 16:08.720
Go back to class.

16:08.720 --> 16:10.940
Oh, can we? Yay!

16:10.940 --> 16:12.950
<b>Student Counseling</b>

16:13.390 --> 16:15.510
Yasuda, we'll come visit again.

16:15.510 --> 16:19.190
Sure, just bring me some cake, too.

16:19.190 --> 16:20.950
<i>What a terrible teacher.</i>

16:20.950 --> 16:24.230
Sensei, we'll come back 
for the cake after school,

16:24.230 --> 16:26.460
so be sure to keep it cold.

16:26.460 --> 16:28.540
I know.

16:36.660 --> 16:38.910
Just what is this?

16:36.970 --> 16:41.470
<b>Science Prep Room</b>

17:02.150 --> 17:05.380
<i>It's nine o'clock
in the student council room.</i>

17:07.200 --> 17:10.000
<i>The door's locked...</i>

17:11.690 --> 17:13.670
<i>and there's a slumbering demon.</i>

17:15.410 --> 17:17.940
<i>How could she fall asleep?</i>

17:18.260 --> 17:19.760
<i>Is it drugs?</i>

17:19.760 --> 17:21.800
<i>Is she taking drugs?!</i>

17:19.760 --> 17:22.770
<b>It's because
the room's so warm</b>

17:23.410 --> 17:28.520
<i>A-Anyway, I'll let the demon sleep.</i>

17:28.520 --> 17:32.280
<i>If I call the school, it should 
ring in the faculty office.</i>

17:32.280 --> 17:34.280
Please Charge

17:34.870 --> 17:36.290
<i>Why?!</i>

17:37.900 --> 17:39.520
Whoa, it's dark.

17:39.520 --> 17:41.990
What's going on? What time is it?

17:41.990 --> 17:43.410
<i>I'm done for.</i>

17:44.390 --> 17:45.440
It seems...

17:45.440 --> 17:51.070
someone locked the door 
while we were sleeping.

17:52.420 --> 17:54.360
How could you let that happen, you idiot?!

17:54.360 --> 17:56.560
Y-You didn't wake up either, Kyo-chan!

17:56.560 --> 17:58.430
Don't put all the blame on me!

17:58.430 --> 18:01.940
Aw, man! I was going to 
buy carrots on the way home!

18:01.940 --> 18:03.430
What am I supposed to do now?!

18:03.430 --> 18:08.220
The gardening club's growing 
a bunch. Just take those.

18:08.220 --> 18:10.330
What kind of council president are you?!

18:10.810 --> 18:13.280
Kyo-chan, your phone! Call someone!

18:13.280 --> 18:15.440
The school! Anyone! Just do it!

18:16.240 --> 18:22.580
<i>R
U
M
B
L
E</i>

18:16.860 --> 18:19.780
Is that how you ask someone to do something?

18:19.780 --> 18:21.330
No, I'm sorry.

18:21.330 --> 18:22.830
But please hurry.

18:22.830 --> 18:24.750
Okay, fine.

18:24.750 --> 18:26.770
Sengoku, what's the school's phone number?

18:27.830 --> 18:31.570
You should have that stored!

18:31.570 --> 18:32.840
Can it.

18:32.840 --> 18:35.180
We just need to check the student handbook.

18:35.180 --> 18:38.340
Right! Now hurry up and call! Make it snappy!

18:38.340 --> 18:40.720
Why are you in such a rush?

18:40.720 --> 18:43.000
You don't need to use the restroom, do you?

18:43.000 --> 18:44.180
Don't copy me.

18:44.180 --> 18:45.470
It's perfectly natural!

18:45.470 --> 18:47.100
Wait, you have to go, too?!

18:48.260 --> 18:51.540
Honestly, what the hell are you two doing?

18:51.540 --> 18:53.730
I was just going home—

18:54.600 --> 18:56.640
Hey, where are you going?!

18:56.640 --> 18:58.030
Where's my thank you?!

18:58.030 --> 18:59.860
<b>Restroom</b>

18:59.860 --> 19:02.370
<b>Student Counseling</b>

19:01.740 --> 19:05.370
So, what were you doing here so late?

19:05.370 --> 19:07.250
He fell asleep.

19:07.250 --> 19:10.270
Hang on. Hori-san was asleep, too.

19:10.270 --> 19:12.570
Are you serious?

19:12.570 --> 19:15.970
You weren't up to something 
inappropriate, were you?

19:15.970 --> 19:17.030
Huh?

19:17.030 --> 19:18.760
What do you mean?

19:18.760 --> 19:25.510
It happens. Students stay
late and start making out.

19:25.510 --> 19:28.890
Hold it! Don't accuse us of that!

19:28.890 --> 19:34.400
And isn't this the fault of whoever locked
 the door without checking inside first?

19:34.400 --> 19:35.750
Hmm? What was that?

19:35.750 --> 19:37.440
I can't hear you.

19:38.490 --> 19:42.490
Well, there are ways 
to figure out what you were up to.

19:43.110 --> 19:46.020
Hori, take off your clothes!

19:46.020 --> 19:49.170
What's going on here, Yasuda-sensei?

19:49.770 --> 19:52.220
Terajima-sensei, you're just in time.

19:52.220 --> 19:54.920
You check Sengoku.

19:54.920 --> 19:56.710
It would be the other way around.

19:56.710 --> 19:58.920
And I'm not checking anyone. 
This is ridiculous.

19:58.920 --> 20:01.850
Checking their lower bodies
will tell us everything.

20:01.850 --> 20:04.140
We won't be doing that.

20:04.140 --> 20:06.850
I certainly hope you haven't used that excuse

20:06.850 --> 20:09.680
to do anything inappropriate 
to female students.

20:12.190 --> 20:14.600
You two may go home.

20:14.600 --> 20:17.800
I need to speak with this perv of a teacher.

20:17.800 --> 20:19.190
Okay!

20:19.190 --> 20:22.460
Terajima-sensei, calling me 
a perv is going too far!

20:19.190 --> 20:28.950
<b>Student Counseling</b>

20:23.000 --> 20:24.830
If you'll excuse us...

20:24.830 --> 20:25.960
Wait, stop!

20:25.960 --> 20:28.950
Now, we're going to go over this in detail.

20:29.850 --> 20:31.350
I need to hurry home.

20:31.900 --> 20:33.850
It's so cold in the hallway.

20:39.710 --> 20:42.720
Huh? You got locked in, Hori-san?

20:43.210 --> 20:44.300
Are you okay?

20:44.300 --> 20:46.380
You could have just called me.

20:46.380 --> 20:48.980
No need. We got out pretty quickly.

20:49.480 --> 20:50.510
Were you alone?

20:50.510 --> 20:51.580
Weren't you scared?

20:51.580 --> 20:54.320
I wasn't alone. Sengoku was there.

21:00.400 --> 21:02.260
President, are you okay?

21:02.260 --> 21:04.290
You were stuck in a room 
with Hori-san, right?

21:04.290 --> 21:06.200
Did she doing anything to you?

21:06.200 --> 21:08.300
I'm fine. Safe and sound.

21:08.300 --> 21:09.320
Hey.

21:10.570 --> 21:13.370
What do you mean by that?

21:13.690 --> 21:16.500
I-I mean, just considering
the power dynamic...

21:16.500 --> 21:17.130
Right?!

21:17.130 --> 21:19.380
Leave me out of this, Miyamura-kun!

21:19.380 --> 21:21.530
I'd like to hear <i>exactly</i> what you mean.

21:21.530 --> 21:24.280
This is what he's talking about, Kyo-chan!

21:25.510 --> 21:27.010
Huh?

21:28.170 --> 21:32.070
Hori-san, you mustn't resort to violence.

21:34.570 --> 21:38.540
Consider anger a chance to improve yourself,

21:38.540 --> 21:40.640
and purge it from your body.

21:43.740 --> 21:45.740
That was Yasuda, right?

21:45.740 --> 21:47.780
It certainly looked like him.

21:48.240 --> 21:53.420
It sounds like he got a talking-to from 
Terajima-sensei and had a change of heart.

21:53.810 --> 21:57.260
That was more than a change of heart!

21:57.260 --> 21:59.250
More like he's been brainwashed.

21:59.650 --> 22:01.930
Terajima-sensei is amazing!

22:01.930 --> 22:02.660
Huh?

22:03.770 --> 22:05.890
Life is precious.

22:07.090 --> 22:09.970
<b>He was back to normal
the next day</b>

23:36.470 --> 23:40.180
Next time
page.10 Jealousy
